139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (   The study examines the impact of urbanisation on child mortality using data from 37 low- and middle-income countries over two decades. It finds that, despite rapid urbanization, rural areas still account for the majority of child deaths. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (   Urban areas, huge cities, show significantly lower child mortality rates compared to rural and smaller urban areas. This is attributed to better healthcare access, higher education levels, and more investments in large cities. However, the mortality gap between rural and urban children remains substantial.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
